; THE EMBER CROWN TOWN HUB (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild) — the realm's heart, and no longer a plan drawn on a
; drawing board.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THIS REPLACED. Four buildings at the corners of a 24 x 16 rectangle, six lamps in three
; mirrored pairs, and every NPC, station, vendor and monument inside that rectangle — a village you
; could read entirely from the middle of it, with a 6.5 m road painted straight through the square.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW. The organising idea is that THE ROAD DOES NOT CROSS THE SQUARE:
;
;   the Kingsway         an S. In from the south at x = -11 (aligned with the Embermarket's Gate Lane
;                        on the far side of the seam), east to the road head at (0, 15) — WHICH IS
;                        WHERE THE PLAYER SPAWNS — north past the square's east flank, then north-west
;                        out to the Crossway at x = -6. Three ground skins, three path segments in
;                        EmberCrown.tres.
;   the road head        z 12..20. The inn, the goods stall, Kael and the guild notice. This is the
;                        first thing a new player sees and it is deliberately a street, not a plaza.
;   the Warband Yard     x -23..-5, z -12..8. The square, WEST of the road and reached by turning off
;                        it: waystone, Solaryn's shrine, the elder, the vault, the apothecary and the
;                        alchemy bench. You cannot see any of it from the spawn.
;   the Craft Yard       x 8..24, z -7..9. The mirror position and deliberately not a mirror shape:
;                        smaller, harder, a working court off the mine road with the smithy closing
;                        its north side, the forge and workbench in the open and Bryn's order bench
;                        against the wall.
;   the Long Green       z -28..-14. A walk under three houses across the north — the approach from
;                        the Crossway gate, and the reason the village reveals itself gradually from
;                        the north instead of all at once.
;   the west and east spurs  z = -4 and z = -2 at the cell edges, feeding Tarn's Landing and the
;                        Emberdeep mine road. Both meet a yard rather than the square.
;
; ⚠️ THE CELL CENTRE DOES NOT MOVE AND NEITHER DO SpawnPoint OR SafeZoneCenter. RegionResource reads
; the spawn at world (0, 1.2, 5) — cell-local (0, 15) — and the cottage property, the safe-zone bubble
; and every fast-travel arrival hang off the same origin. The Kingsway was drawn THROUGH that point on
; purpose; everything else in the cell moved around it.
;
; ⚠️ FIVE SCHEDULES WERE MIGRATED WITH THIS REBUILD. Elder, Innkeeper, VendorAlch, VendorGoods and
; VendorSmith author RAW WORLD destinations (Origin is zero on all five, unlike the Embermarket's,
; which are cell-local), and this cell sits at world (0, 0, -10). So a point read out of this file is
; world = local + (0, 0, -10), and getting that backwards is the 37C placement bug in miniature.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav; actors and interactables do not. Geometry outside the
; NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the navmesh, and a body inside it is a hole in everyone
; else's paths.
;
; ⚠️ THE ROAD AND YARD SKINS HAVE NO COLLIDERS. They are 6 cm slabs. The Embermarket's Salt Steps are
; the one piece of raised ground in the realm; this cell is flat and its verticality comes from
; fourteen buildings and their silhouettes.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. agent_* dims still sit on the voxel grid to avoid precision warnings.
[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_hub"]
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.3
cell_height = 0.3
agent_height = 1.75
agent_radius = 0.5
agent_max_climb = 0.5
agent_max_slope = 42.0

