; ⚠️ 38R PUTS THE CONVERSATION BACK, AND THE ServiceComponent IS GONE RATHER THAN BESIDE IT.
; 38D replaced the placeholder conversation with a ServiceComponent because an entity gets ONE
; interactable — EntityNode.GetComponent returns the first child match — and left a note that the
; trade-and-talk question was 38E's. 38E answered it for shops (DialogueEffect.OpenShop) and said
; the same answer was owed to services; DialogueEffect.OpenService is that answer, so the bed is
; bought through the door choice in dialogue.innkeeper and the walk-up prompt is retired.
;
; ⚠️ The two must NOT sit side by side: with both here the Dialogue node above would win and the
; service would be silent forever, which is the exact fault this comment has now described twice.
; ⚠️ And the bed is now reachable ONLY through this graph — a broken dialogue id here is not a
; missing conversation, it is the only inn in the realm closing.
[node name="Dialogue" type="Node" parent="Innkeeper"]
script = ExtResource("7_dialogue")
DialogueId = "dialogue.innkeeper"

[node name="Schedule" type="Node" parent="Innkeeper"]
script = ExtResource("8_schedule")
ScheduleId = "schedule.innkeeper"

