; --- 38Q: Bryn's order bench ------------------------------------------------
; The commission counter. Everything above it in this block is FREE — the forge eight metres away is
; a public station and always has been — and that contrast is the feature rather than a problem with
; it: the bench charges for the materials the player did not bring, and for nothing else the forge
; would have done for them.
;
; ⚠️ A SEPARATE ENTITY FROM BRYN, AND FORCED. An entity gets one interactable and he carries a
; DialogueComponent holding his shop and his quest, so a ServiceComponent on him would never fire.
; 38P split a broker and her clerk for the same reason and it read better than it deserved: you talk
; to the man, and you leave an order at the bench.
;
; Parented to Nav rather than to the root like the three stations above it, so its collider is inside
; the NavigationRegion3D. NOW.md invariant 15: a collider outside it blocks the player while the
; navmesh stays ignorant of it, and Bryn's routine walks him past this spot twice a day.
;
; ⚠️ Yaw 0 and this model are the RENDERED answers, not the reasoned ones. The table runs east-west
; so its long side faces the square the player walks in from, and Bryn stands off its west end —
; the smith behind his counter. See the shape comment above for the prop that was rejected on sight.
[node name="OrderBench" type="Node3D" parent="Nav"]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, 0, 11.5, 0, 4.5)
script = ExtResource("1_entity")
DisplayName = "Bryn's Order Bench"

[node name="Collider" type="StaticBody3D" parent="Nav/OrderBench"]

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="Nav/OrderBench/Collider"]
